IMPORT `dg-core`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, ss 321(b), 376(b), 381(d) and 382(c):
-- SERVICE OF PROCESS ON THE SECRETARY OF STATE -- what the four passages share.
--
-- Four sections let process be served on the Secretary of State and then say, in almost the same words,
-- what the Secretary of State must send the corporation, what the plaintiff must do and pay, what record
-- the Secretary of State keeps and for how long. The text is repeated, so the rules are written once here,
-- under the first section that says it (s 321(b)); each of the other three sections has its own rule in its
-- own module that calls these with its own address condition and carries its own citation.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation (an incorporator, a director
-- or officer, a stockholder). Here the person is the one the letter is addressed to (a director or officer of
-- the corporation) or the plaintiff (a stockholder suing, for example).
-- Dialect: the stable build 1.6.98; no section GIVEN, no REFUSE, every NOT bracketed.

§ `s 321(b) The letter, the plaintiff's steps and the record`

-- The Secretary of State's duty to notify the corporation (owed to the corporation; the person is told by letter).
-- src:1636 | In the event that service is effected through the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation by letter, directed to the corporation at its principal place of business as it appears on the records relating to such corporation on file with the Secretary of State or, if no such address appears, at its last registered office. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served …
-- src:1878 | In the event that service is effected through the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation by letter, directed to the corporation at its principal place of business as it appears on the last annual report filed pursuant to § 374 of this title or, if no such address appears, at its last registered office. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served …
-- src:1914 | In the event of service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with subsection (c) of this section, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation by letter, directed to the corporation at the address stated in the certificate which was filed by the corporation with the Secretary of State pursuant to subsection (a) of this section. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served …
-- src:1920 | In the event of service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with subsection (a) of this section, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation thereof by letter, directed to the corporation at the address furnished to the Secretary of State by the plaintiff in such action, suit or proceeding. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(b) (src:1636); § 376(b) (src:1878); § 381(d) (src:1914); § 382(c) (src:1920)
DECLARE `s 321(b) Letter from the Secretary of State` HAS
    `the Secretary of State sent the letter forthwith`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the letter was sent by mail or courier with a record of mailing or deposit and a record of delivery signed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State`           IS A BOOLEAN

-- The address condition differs from section to section and is computed by the section's own rule.
-- src:1636 | In the event that service is effected through the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation by letter, directed to the corporation at its principal place of business as it appears on the records relating to such corporation on file with the Secretary of State or, if no such address appears, at its last registered office. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(b) (src:1636)
GIVEN `the letter` IS A `s 321(b) Letter from the Secretary of State`
      `the letter was addressed as the section requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(b) the Secretary of State's letter meets the section` `the letter` `the letter was addressed as the section requires` MEANS
        `the letter`'s `the Secretary of State sent the letter forthwith`
    AND `the letter was addressed as the section requires`
    AND `the letter`'s `the letter was sent by mail or courier with a record of mailing or deposit and a record of delivery signed`
    AND `the letter`'s `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State`

-- src:1636 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, …
-- src:1878 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, …
-- src:1914 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being made pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, …
-- src:1920 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being made pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(b) (src:1636); § 376(b) (src:1878); § 381(d) (src:1914); § 382(c) (src:1920)
DECLARE `s 321(b) Plaintiff's steps` HAS
    `the plaintiff served the process and any other papers in duplicate`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the plaintiff notified the Secretary of State that service was being effected so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State for the use of the State`    IS A NUMBER

-- The text calls these the plaintiff's DUTY; it does not say that failing them makes the service ineffective, so the
-- rules below say whether the plaintiff has done what is required and do not feed the effectiveness of the service
-- (fork F31).
-- The fee is "as prescribed under s 391(a)(29)" of this title.
-- src:1636 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(b) (src:1636)
GIVEN steps IS A `s 321(b) Plaintiff's steps`
      `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 391(a)(29) (piece dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(b) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` steps `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)` MEANS
        steps's `the plaintiff served the process and any other papers in duplicate`
    AND steps's `the plaintiff notified the Secretary of State that service was being effected so`
    AND steps's `the amount the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State for the use of the State` AT LEAST `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)`

-- "which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding if the plaintiff shall prevail therein"
