    AND record's `the record gives the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding`
    AND record's `the record gives the fact that service has been effected through the Secretary of State`
    AND record's `the record gives the return date`
    AND record's `the record gives the day and hour when the service was made`

-- "The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information for a period longer than 5 years
-- from receipt of the service of process." Reading (fork F1): the last day of the 5 years is the fifth anniversary of
-- the receipt, and the Secretary of State must still retain the record on that day.
-- src:1636 | The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information for a period longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 321(b) (src:1636)
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` IS A DATE
      `the date the record is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 321(b) the Secretary of State must still retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` `the date the record is asked about` MEANS
    `the date the record is asked about` AT MOST (`the date` (`period in years` 5) `after` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process`)
